            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp",
            "name": "Focus Gaze",
            "sort": 1400000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 1
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The kophos stares at a creature it can see within 30 feet. The target must immediately attempt a Will save against silent agony. If the creature fails its save and was already stupefied, it instead begins craving pain at the hands of the kophos, taking a –2 circumstance penalty to AC against the kophos's attacks for as long as it remains stupefied. After attempting this save, the creature is then temporarily immune to Focus Gaze (but not the normal silent agony aura) until the start of the kophos's next turn.</p>"
